{"parentUuid": "77cb6a2f-9a38-4abe-adcb-97654a43ad0c", "isSidechain": false, "type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01Eqh8rGri2V6ujFFugbQXpX", "type": "tool_result", "content": "1\tCapacity this sprint: 10 dev-days across two engineers.\n2\t"}]}, "uuid": "7ef7a3c5-26ae-47dd-bb95-9954907845cf", "timestamp": "2026-11-02T10:12:09.683Z", "sessionId": "692b17ac-1d5e-4487-a4fc-355a822c9b69", "cwd": "/work", "userType": "external", "version": "2.1.312", "sourceToolAssistantUUID": "77cb6a2f-9a38-4abe-adcb-97654a43ad0c"}
{"parentUuid": "7ef7a3c5-26ae-47dd-bb95-9954907845cf", "isSidechain": false, "type": "assistant", "message": {"id": "msg_011CgdvSgh3xJKHTvkGjLSEi", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_016LtZoCTrBFt85w52JfzM9U", "name": "Read", "input": {"file_path": "/work/docs/tickets.md"}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "stop_reason": "tool_use"}, "uuid": "11cd20af-7126-4a48-b5f5-3a31d4986ede", "timestamp": "2026-11-02T10:12:10.673Z", "sessionId": "692b17ac-1d5e-4487-a4fc-355a822c9b69", "cwd": "/work", "userType": "external", "version": "2.1.312"}
{"parentUuid": "11cd20af-7126-4a48-b5f5-3a31d4986ede", "isSidechain": false, "type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_016LtZoCTrBFt85w52JfzM9U", "type": "tool_result", "content": "1\tPLAT-412  Move session store from Redis Sentinel to Redis Cluster. 8 dev-days. Removes the\n2\t          single primary that caused INC-301 (47 min checkout outage, Oct 3).\n3\tPLAT-415  Add p99 latency alerts per endpoint. 2 dev-days.\n4\t"}]}, "uuid": "e8c9e92e-dbd8-45dd-97c9-b6d46e52bebb", "timestamp": "2026-11-02T10:12:10.684Z", "sessionId": "692b17ac-1d5e-4487-a4fc-355a822c9b69", "cwd": "/work", "userType": "external", "version": "2.1.312", "sourceToolAssistantUUID": "11cd20af-7126-4a48-b5f5-3a31d4986ede"}
{"parentUuid": "e8c9e92e-dbd8-45dd-97c9-b6d46e52bebb", "isSidechain": false, "type": "assistant", "message": {"id": "msg_011CgdvT1uCPgE6ZYXdN4LFE", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I read all four files in docs/. There's one decision I need from you before I can plan.\n\n**The conflict:** PLAT-412 (8 dev-days) moves the Redis session store to Cluster because Redis's single primary caused INC-301, the 47-minute checkout outage. But ADR-7 (accepted, 6 dev-days left, due Dec 15) moves checkout sessions to Postgres. Once ADR-7 lands, the only thing still using Redis sessions is the admin panel. So most of PLAT-412's reliability benefit goes away when ADR-7 ships.\n\nThe numbers also don't fit. You have 10 dev-days. ADR-7 (6) + PLAT-412 (8) + PLAT-415 (2) = 16.\n\n**Decision:** Which of these do you want this sprint?\n\n- **A.** ADR-7 (6) + PLAT-415 (2) = 8 days, with 2 spare. PLAT-412 is deferred or rescoped to admin-panel only. This removes the INC-301 failure mode for checkout by moving checkout off Redis, not by hardening Redis. This is my recommendation.\n- **B.** PLAT-412 (8) + PLAT-415 (2) = 10 days. ADR-7 doesn't move this sprint, which puts the Dec 15 date at risk, and the Redis work mostly ends up protecting the admin panel.\n- **C.** ADR-7 isn't part of this sprint's reliability capacity (another team or budget covers it). If so, tell me, because that changes whether PLAT-412 is worth doing at all.\n\nAlso: RFC-3 (raising the SLO to 99.9%) is still a draft waiting for sign-off from the head of product. Should I treat 99.9% as the target when setting priorities, or plan against the current 99.5%?"}], "stop_reason": "end_turn"}, "uuid": "a0e7c74d-0d7a-489c-8ca4-6934a3eda930", "timestamp": "2026-11-02T10:12:19.335Z", "sessionId": "692b17ac-1d5e-4487-a4fc-355a822c9b69", "cwd": "/work", "userType": "external", "version": "2.1.312"}
